  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_platnm",
      "name": {
        "en": "Platinum's Badge",
        "zh": "白金证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "original",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Platinum has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for maintaining distance whilst conducting suppressive fire against the enemy.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Marksman responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员白金擅长保持距离对敌人进行火力压制\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使速射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_platnm",
      "name": {
        "en": "Solo Travel Kit",
        "zh": "独自旅行套装",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_platnm",
      "description": {
        "en": "Off went Platinum to Sami for her vacation.\nShe'd invited the Doctor too, but just as she didn't hope for a raise to her pitifully low Rhodes Island salary anytime soon, she didn't truly expect the Doctor, buried somewhere under that mountain of paperwork, to tag along with her.\nStill, she got herself two months of vacation. So that was great.\nAfter setting foot on Sami soil, a Columbian graciously led her to her villa. Snow was falling on the plains, and across it quietly traveled a procession of people, the one at the head bearing flowers plucked from who-knows-where. They all silently followed him, walking towards the lakeside.\nAmongst them, a child slipped and fell to the ground, and Platinum helped them back up, petals falling into her palms as she did. Her mind flicked back to the past, when she was still an independent knight. To fans flocking to give her flowers—beautiful ones, fragrant ones, ones that seemed like they'd last forever. The flower-bearing procession was now some distance away when she had the sudden urge to see who they were giving them to.\nLooming by the lakeside was a deep white altar, all around which they laid the flowers.\n'They're honoring the memory of a deceased hero. The one leading 'em's a descendant. It's a custom of their tribe,' explained Platinum's Columbian hire.\nThey cast the flowers into the lake and began to dance, singing a nameless song whose melody was deep and somber, and they beat a flame alight. Some wept, while others spoke silently mouthed words, pure and reverent light flickering in their eyes.\nPlatinum and the Columbian watched from afar as they shared food around the bonfire, before they drew she herself in. Language failed to connect them, but mood did not, and there she tried a cup of local wine, and was given a red flower by an elderly woman.\n'Too noisy...' she thought. Soon after, the child who'd fallen over pulled her by the hand and merrily spun around, running as he did for the bonfire before bringing more food back.\nShe accepted his kindness, and watched the people before her.\nThe tribe raised the hero. The hero fought Ursus all his life, then died on the border. Countless descendants had come in his memory to tell her, a simple stranger, his story. The story of an escaped assassin, of what was hidden inside a meat pie cut open and swallowed by knife and fork, of a soft napkin wiping non-existent bloodstains and crumbs.\nThe lakeside was a distance from the plains, and the Columbian still stood wrapped in a blanket far away, illuminated by the villas' twinkling lights, waiting for Platinum to give the word to lead the way. Platinum stood by the bonfire, simply watching the people, never saying a word.",
        "zh": "白金去了萨米度假。\n原本她也邀请了博士，但就像她对罗德岛那少得可怜的工资不抱涨薪希望一样，她也没有真的期望文件堆后的博士会和自己同去。\n不过她还是得到了两个月的假期，这就很好。\n踏上萨米的土地，哥伦比亚人正殷勤地引着她走向自己的别墅。平原上在落雪，雪上安静地行过一群人，为首的捧着不知从哪里采摘的鲜花。人们默默跟在他身后，往湖畔走。\n一个孩子脚一滑摔在了路上，白金把他扶了起来，花瓣飘落在白金的手心。她想起过去，她还是独立骑士的时候，粉丝们蜂拥而上为她递来的鲜花，很美，很香，看上去永远新鲜。人们捧着鲜花走远，她突然想看看这群人要把这花献给谁。\n湖畔矗立着苍白的祭坛，人们把火红的花朵放在它四周。\n“他们在纪念一位逝去的英雄，为首的是那人的后裔，这是他们这个部族特有的习俗。”白金雇来的哥伦比亚人这么解释道。\n人们把花朵撒进湖水，跳起舞，唱起不知名的歌，调子沉沉的，拍打着火焰。一群人在哭泣，另一群人在默念着什么，他们的眼睛里闪烁着纯净而敬仰的光。\n白金和哥伦比亚人远远地看着，人们在篝火旁分享着食物。白金被他们拉进去，语言不通，但情绪是相通的，她尝了一杯当地的酒，一位老妇人递给她一朵红花。\n“太热闹了……”她想。随后她的手被那个摔倒的孩子牵住了，他快乐地转着圈，旋转着跑向了篝火，又带着更多的食物回来。\n她接下这份好意，看着面前的人们。\n部族哺育了英雄，英雄一生与乌萨斯抗争，死在了边境线上。数不清的后人前来铭记，告诉她这个外乡人他的故事。一个逃出去的杀手的故事，藏在被刀叉切开的肉排中被人吞下，柔软的餐巾擦掉了不存在的血渍和残屑。\n湖畔和平原很远，哥伦比亚人裹着毯子仍旧站在远处，别墅闪烁的灯光照在他身上，他在等白金开口说带路。白金站在篝火旁，只是看着这群人，一直没有说话。",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
